chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Recognizing text in images for an advanced course: chapter 22 and today's Tesseract, pytesseract, NAPS2 and OCRmyPDF"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-13T16:52:13; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.6." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 22 of the 3rd edition teach about reading text from images with the Tesseract engine and pytesseract (installing, the four lines that read an image, accuracy and preprocessing, other languages, a language model that fixes mistakes) and about making searchable PDFs with NAPS2, which of its printed outputs, listings and statements still hold under Python 3.14.6 with pytesseract 0.3.13 and Pillow 12.3.0, with the pytesseract 0.3.10 and Pillow 10.4.0 that its Appendix A pins, and with the Tesseract builds a reader may have, and what must an advanced course correct or add so that it matches the engines, the data files and the files the book ships?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-13." .
