chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 22 of the 3rd edition, Recognizing Text in Images, teaches PyTesseract and the Tesseract OCR engine (four lines to read an image, preprocessing advice, a large language model to fix mistakes, other languages) and the NAPS2 application run from Python for PDFs with embedded text, and ends with 7 practice questions and 1 practice program, the Browser Text Scraper [P01]. The page was fetched on 2026-10-13 and returned 200 with 40,521 bytes, holds 8 listings and 2 figures, and its sha256 equals the chapterDigest the book's own chapter ontology records [P01] [P03] [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P03, chx:P04 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The online materials"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The online materials of the 3rd edition (7,759,877 bytes, 91 files, 72 of them Python) hold ocr-example.png (939 by 1198, mode RGBA), frankenstein.png (1130 by 672, mode P), frankenstein_jpn.png (1211 by 606, mode RGB) and preprocess_ocr.py (190 lines), and none of ocrscreen.py, output.pdf, cat.png, dog.png, moose.png, spam.pdf, eggs.pdf or output.txt, which the chapter creates or assumes; the publisher's book page has 1 occurrence of Recognizing Text and 0 of Tesseract, OCR or NAPS2 [P01] [P02] [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P04 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The chapter replayed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Of the 22 statements of the chapter's listings 1, 2, 4, 5 and 6 replayed as printed, 18 matched the book with the apt Tesseract 5.3.4, 20 with 5.5.3 and the fast data, 20 with 4.1.1, 18 with 5.5.3 and the best data, 19 with all the apt languages and 21 with all languages under 5.5.3; with the book's pins, 18 matched on Python 3.13.14, 8 on Python 3.14.6 and 0 in an empty Python; the statements that differ are get_languages(), the first word Iv, the Japanese heading and the English gibberish [P01] [P05]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P05 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The pin that cannot import"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Appendix A pins pytesseract==0.3.10, whose source imports pkgutil.find_loader, removed in Python 3.14, so on Python 3.14.6 the import raises ImportError (cannot import name 'find_loader' from 'pkgutil'), on 3.13.14 it only warns, and 0.3.13 has no find_loader; PyPI has 28 releases of pytesseract, none numbered 0.3.11 or 0.3.12, and three older ones (0.3.4, 0.3.7 and 0.3.8) install only from source [P05] [P19] [P28]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P05, chx:P19, chx:P28 .
chx:F5 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The same page, different engines"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The first word of frankenstein.png came back as Iv with 4.1.1 and 5.5.3 and the fast data, In with the apt 5.3.4, Ir with the best data of all three and It with the legacy data under 4.1.1 and 5.5.3, where the book prints Iv; the character error rate against the page was 0.0035 with the fast data and 0.0017 with the best and the legacy data (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract versions named); the picture shows an I followed by a small capital T [P01] [P10] [P16] [P17]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P10, chx:P16, chx:P17 .
chx:F6 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The three kinds of English data"@en ; sen0414:findingText "eng.traineddata is 4,113,088 bytes in tessdata_fast, 15,400,601 in tessdata_best and 23,466,654 in tessdata, each equal to the file its GitHub repository serves on 2026-10-13, and the apt package's file is the fast one; all of tessdata_fast is 706,776,225 bytes (126 languages and 37 script models), where the chapter says all languages add about 600MB [P01] [P10] [P16] [P17]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P10, chx:P16, chx:P17 .
chx:F7 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Language codes"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter calls the language strings ISO 639-3 codes while the Tesseract manual page says ISO 639-2; 13 of the 126 names of tessdata_fast are not three letters, osd is no language, lang='ger' (the bibliographic 639-2 code of German) raises TesseractError while lang='deu' reads, lang='Japanese' raises the same error, and a missing pack inside 'eng+xyz' raises nothing and reads at 0.0116 [P01] [P14] [P31] [P32]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P14, chx:P31, chx:P32 .
chx:F8 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The Japanese page"@en ; sen0414:findingText "On frankenstein_jpn.png (1211 by 606, 13 lines) the picture shows 第 5 章 and 憂鬱; the apt Tesseract with lang='jpn' printed 第 5 剖 and 愛鬱 where the book prints 第 5 剖 and 芝鬱, the fast data under 5.5.3 equalled the book and the best data gave 901 characters against 538; lang='eng' gave 0 Japanese characters and gibberish, and 'eng+jpn' read a mixed line correctly [P01]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F9 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "What hurts"@en ; sen0414:findingText "On drawn pages with known text the apt Tesseract read 8-pixel letters at 0.2278 and 12-pixel letters at 0.0193, a page turned by 2 degrees at 0.0154 and by 5 degrees at 0.5753, noise of deviation 60 at 0.1313 and of 90 at 1.0 (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract version 5.3.4); white text on black read at 0.0116 because tessedit_do_invert is 1 (deprecated, to go in release 6) and at 1.0965 with it off, so the chapter's advice of dark text on light describes what the engine did not need [P01] [P08]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P08 .
chx:F10 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "What helps"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Enlarging a 9-pixel page 2 times lowered the error rate from 0.0579 to 0.0154, deskewing a page turned by 6 degrees (estimated -6.0) from 0.5985 to 0.0116, Otsu thresholding raised 0.0154 to 0.0347 on a noisy page, a tight crop returned the empty string and the same crop with a 10-pixel white border returned the line, and telling the engine 300 dpi for a 9-pixel page raised 0.0579 to 0.7452 (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract version 5.3.4) [P01] [P08] [P43]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P08, chx:P43 .
chx:F11 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Segmentation"@en ; sen0414:findingText "--psm 3, 4, 6 and 11 read a page of 6 lines at 0.0116 and --psm 7 and 13 at 0.9923 and 0.9961; two columns read column by column with the default mode and merged line by line with --psm 6, and columns 2 and 4 pixels apart merged at 0.5819 and 0.5791; tesseract --help-psm lists 14 modes, and the chapter uses none of the words psm, dpi, whitelist or timeout (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract version 5.3.4) [P01] [P14]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P14 .
chx:F12 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Errors a spell checker cannot see"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The 2 wrong words of the 106 on Figure 22-1 (IT as In, motion as Motion) are real English words and a spell check against the 104,334 words of /usr/share/dict/words flagged nothing; the mean confidence was 94.5, the wrong In had 55 and Motion 92; the language model step was NOT EXECUTED, and its sample prompt has 419 characters [P01]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F13 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Hyphens at the line ends"@en ; sen0414:findingText "ocr-example.png gave 51 lines with 7 words hyphenated at a line end (dig-ital, pro-grams, compre-hend, pro-grams, straight-forward, pro-gramming and graph-ics); removing every hyphen at a line end turned the real compound well-known into wellknown in a sample, so a word list is needed [P01]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F14 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "NAPS2"@en ; sen0414:findingText "NAPS2 8.5.1 (the .deb package) ran the book's call with naps2_path = ['naps2', 'console'] (return code 0, 1 page, text error rate 0.0035) with its own Tesseract 5.5.0; a second call without -f returned 0 and printed File already exists. Use --force to overwrite.; the Windows path and flatpak raised FileNotFoundError; -i spam.pdf[0:2], spam.pdf[-2:] and spam.pdf[1:6:2] gave the pages 0 and 1, 5 and 6, and 1, 3 and 5 (MEASURED single run with the Tesseract version 5.5.0) [P01] [P22] [P23]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P22, chx:P23 .
chx:F15 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Searchable PDFs"@en ; sen0414:findingText "A PDF that Pillow made from frankenstein.png held 0 characters of text, the PDF of image_to_pdf_or_hocr read at 0.0138 with 106 word boxes, and ocrmypdf 17.13.0 exited 2 for a PNG without a resolution, 0 with --image-dpi 150 (0.0035), 6 for a PDF that already has text and 0 with --skip-text (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract version 5.3.4) [P24] [P25]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P24, chx:P25 .
chx:F16 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The screen scraper"@en ; sen0414:findingText "On a virtual X display the template's own constants (400, 200, 1000, 800) cropped 600 by 600 pixels and appended 361 characters (0.3824 against the page), the whole window gave 581 characters at 0.0035 and a second run made 1162 in all; without DISPLAY the import raised KeyError: 'DISPLAY'; nobody saw the screen (MEASURED single runs with the Tesseract version 5.3.4) [P01] [P33]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P33 .
chx:F17 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The shipped script and the linked post"@en ; sen0414:findingText "preprocess_ocr.py (190 lines) calls FileNotFileError, grayscale_image and open_image, which it never defines, defines a function named open, and ends with NameError: name 'open_image' is not defined when run; the post at autbor.com/preprocessingocr answered 301 and then 200 and says it is a placeholder [P01] [P02] [P41]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P41 .
chx:F18 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Interpreters and releases"@en ; sen0414:findingText "One program of 19 items printed the same under 11 interpreters (Python 3.11.17 to 3.15.0b4); 9 items printed the same under 14 Pillow releases (9.5.0 to 12.3.0); between pytesseract 0.3.9, 0.3.10 and 0.3.13 only the confidence type changed, a str in 0.3.9 and an int from 0.3.10 [P19] [P44] [P50]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P19, chx:P44, chx:P50 .
chx:F19 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Not executed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Nothing ran on Windows or macOS, with Homebrew, with the Flatpak of NAPS2, with a flatbed scanner, with a large language model or on a real screen with a real browser; Python 3.15 was only a beta (3.15.0b4); the repository commit the course pins was not opened; and the photograph of the stories was not fetched because the single request to Wikimedia Commons answered 429 [P01] [P23] [P50]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P23, chx:P50 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "39 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "53 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-10-13T16:52:13; 23 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
